# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# NOTE: .gitignore does NOT apply to a Docker build context — this file is the only one consulted.
# That is why build/, .svelte-kit/ and src/lib/paraglide/ are listed here even though git already
# ignores all three.

# ── Installed / generated trees ──────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules
.svelte-kit
build

# Regenerated by paraglideVitePlugin during `vite build` (vite.config.ts), so a stale host copy
# has no business travelling in. Verified that the recompile really happens inside the container:
# changing a value in messages/en.json and rebuilding WITHOUT running `paraglide-js compile` on
# the host produced the new string in the container's prerendered HTML.
src/lib/paraglide

# ── Test and tooling output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Measured: test-results 8.9M, and nothing in `npm run build` reads any of it.
test-results
playwright-report
coverage

# ── Repo furniture the build never reads ─────────────────────────────────────
# .claude is 5.8M of PRP/plan/report history.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude

# ── Secrets and local noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `vite build` LOADS .env files and PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the client bundle, so a
# developer's local .env must not reach a build layer. Everything the image legitimately needs
# at build time arrives as an ARG — see the Dockerfile's build stage. .env.example is kept
# because it is documentation, not configuration.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*
